# AG-3 Backup Monitoring with Wazuh

## Overview

Wazuh was configured to monitor the backup log from APP01.

The monitored log is:

```bash
/var/log/nextcloud-backup.log
```

This allows Wazuh to detect both successful and failed backup events.

## Failed Backup Monitoring

A custom Wazuh rule was created:

```xml
<rule id="100100" level="12">
  <match>BACKUP_FAILED</match>
  <description>AG3 Nextcloud automated backup failed on APP01</description>
  <group>backup_failure,</group>
</rule>
```

To test a real backup failure, the MinIO access key was temporarily changed to an invalid value.

The backup failed and the script recorded:

```text
BACKUP_FAILED Restic backup failed
```

Wazuh detected this event using rule:

```text
100100
```

## Successful Backup Monitoring

A second Wazuh rule was created:

```xml
<rule id="100101" level="3">
  <match>BACKUP_SUCCESS</match>
  <description>AG3 Nextcloud automated backup completed successfully on APP01</description>
  <group>backup_success,</group>
</rule>
```

When a backup completes successfully, Wazuh detects:

```text
BACKUP_SUCCESS
```

using rule:

```text
100101
```

## Wazuh Dashboard

Two metric visualisations were created.

Successful backup filter:

```text
rule.id:100101
```

Failed backup filter:

```text
rule.id:100100
```

This allows the dashboard to show both successful and failed backup events.

## Connection Issue

During testing, some alerts were not received because the Wazuh Manager PC entered sleep mode.

After keeping the Wazuh Manager PC awake, the connection remained stable and the alerts were received correctly.
